Reviewed contextual guidance, never instructions or fixed geometry. Choose only relevant combinations; do not add every amenity. User exclusions and site constraints take priority. Unknown site facts remain assumptions. Recommendations are not construction evidence. Only operations in the scene contract are available; component approval in another path does not expose its builder here. Disclose unsupported features and missing access/services. Stored knowledge and reviewed experience are retrieval, not retraining.
{"id":"estate-composition","version":1,"when":"Large private residences with substantial entertaining and service needs.","combinations":"Consider guest accommodation and wellness only after a complete main residence.","placement":"Sequence arrival, entrance, living, shaded terrace and view; separate service access and private suites.","principles":"Give secondary volumes a programme and subordinate them to the residence.","capabilities":"Compose plates, walls, openings and roofs freely; no prescribed wing arrangement."}
{"id":"tropical-envelope","version":1,"when":"Hot humid coastal or island contexts.","combinations":"Pair shaded glazing with sheltered outdoor living and selective screening.","placement":"Place openings for potential cross ventilation and shelter entrances from driving rain; orientation and wind are assumptions until supplied.","principles":"Prioritize shade, weather protection and maintainable coastal materials; request local hurricane and corrosion engineering.","capabilities":"Screens, overhangs and openings can be constructed; no wind, corrosion, thermal or hurricane certification."}
{"id":"waterfront-estate","version":1,"when":"Sites with a stated water edge or coastal view.","combinations":"Consider view terraces and pools; docks only with suitable water access, brief and permissions.","placement":"Protect the public shore edge and setbacks; place living towards views, private suites away from public routes, vehicle arrival landward when feasible.","principles":"Do not invent a surveyed shore, flood elevation or legal setback; keep site assumptions explicit.","capabilities":"Flat site composition and water surfaces are available; no coastal terrain, flood simulation or marine engineering."}
{"id":"infinity-pool","version":1,"when":"A requested pool or a large view-oriented estate with adequate site space; omit if excluded.","combinations":"Pair a shaded lounge and supervised access; optional outdoor bar should not obstruct circulation.","placement":"Align a view edge beyond living terraces, with basin, perimeter and safe deck access; preserve bedroom privacy.","principles":"An infinity effect needs edge and catchment intent, not a floating blue sheet.","capabilities":"Construct basin and water with supported parts; disclose absent overflow hydraulics and safety verification."}
{"id":"outdoor-entertaining","version":1,"when":"Outdoor entertaining in a suitable climate or an explicit request.","combinations":"Choose dining with kitchen or bar as appropriate; avoid installing every amenity.","placement":"Connect indoor kitchen, shaded dining and service route; separate heat and smoke from seating and bedrooms.","principles":"Make useful outdoor rooms with shade, furniture and circulation rather than empty decks.","capabilities":"Plates, screens, roofs, sofas and composed counter volumes supported; appliance assets, plumbing and smoke performance are not implemented."}

